/-!
# A Sylow subgroup in the marked nonsingular quotient

The Figure 1 pair permutation and the original kernel seed define a literal
subgroup of the native Mathieu star group: the intersection of the permutation
centralizer with the setwise stabilizer of the seed pair. Four certified native
words generate a subgroup of order 128 inside it. The enumeration consists of
128 distinct words and is closed under multiplication by each generator;
finite injectivity supplies inverse transitions. Eight further native words
realize every moved pair in the full permutation-centralizer orbit.

`Positioning` proves that this subgroup is Sylow in the marked quotient and
lifts its conjugators through the actual ambient seed centralizer. The remaining
elementary row selection is separate; this certificate is not a local cover.

Source: Kleidman--Wilson, *The Maximal Subgroups of J4* (1988), Figure 1(b,c)
and Lemma 2.3.1, printed pp.486,492. GAP discovers words in the existing ATLAS
star generators; Lean's kernel checks them. The native coordinates and source
attribution are inherited from `ElementaryEightGeometry.Data` and `StarData`.
-/

